    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d563">

                <pb facs="0563" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.72 AL 5/39: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gade</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-04-26T12:00:00-05:00">April 26,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:59 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>38. General Enriquez<anchor n="52" xml:id="d563-f1"/> last night gave All America
                    Cables an ultimatum requiring payment of $354,000 as settlement of alleged back
                    taxes. If ultimatum which expires on Thursday is not accepted he <pb facs="0564"
                        n="555" xml:id="pg555"/> threatens to seize the Company’s properties.
                        Roosevelt,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d563-f2"/> the Vice President of the
                    company, has requested no action from the Legation but merely wishes to keep it
                    informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gade</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
